{"timestamp": 1779396577.972146, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Wait, look at the actual votes being cast \u2014 Alice and Eve already locked in on me instantly, no deliberation. That's classic duck coordination. And Diana, Frank \u2014 I misspoke, I said \"checking\" because I was tapping the panel trying to figure out what task was even there. I'm not a Goose pretending, I just used a bad word under pressure when I'm being accused of murder. Cut me some slack.\n\nHere's what I actually saw with my own eyes: at tick 13, Eve was in weapons and left toward security right as I walked in from cafeteria. Charlie was alive. I tapped the panel, turned around, and Alice walked in seconds later yelling. The timing only works if Eve killed Charlie on her way out and Alice happened to walk in right after me \u2014 OR Alice killed him and is framing me as the convenient scapegoat she \"found.\"\n\nThink about it: Alice's route conveniently ends at the body. Eve's route conveniently passes through weapons at the exact tick of the murder. They're both vouching for each other's early game but neither has an alibi for the kill window. I'm one person against a coordinated story.\n\nI'm voting Eve. She was the last one alone with Charlie before me."}}
